cff-version: 1.2.0
title: mental-health-guard-harness
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. Please also
  cite the MindGuard paper listed under `references`, whose method this harness
  implements.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Weald
    given-names: Ryan
repository-code: "https://github.com/rally-dfs/mental-health-guard-harness"
abstract: >-
  A research harness for training and evaluating turn-level safety classifiers on
  multi-turn mental health conversations: synthetic conversation generation, judge
  labeling with majority voting, LoRA fine-tuning, and log-probability-based scoring
  with AUROC and FPR-at-fixed-TPR metrics.
keywords:
  - safety-classification
  - mental-health
  - llm-evaluation
  - knowledge-distillation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.1
references:
  - type: article
    title: "MindGuard: Guardrail Classifiers for Multi-Turn Mental Health Support"
    authors:
      - family-names: Farinhas
        name-suffix: et al.
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.48550/arXiv.2602.00950
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.00950"
    notes: >-
      The method this harness implements. Licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; no text, prompts,
      models, or evaluation data from that work are included in this repository.
